  "caption": "T15. Mean dry-season daytime LST of West Java from Terra and Aqua, with Sen's slope. Both satellites have drifted from their nominal overpass times in their final years, so part of any trend can be orbital.",
  "image": "images/real/t15-lst.png",
  "live": "import io\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nDATA = \"\"\"lst,sensor,year\n29.891,Terra (≈10:30),2003\n29.131,Terra (≈10:30),2004\n28.206,Terra (≈10:30),2005\n30.188,Terra (≈10:30),2006\n29.212,Terra (≈10:30),2007\n29.984,Terra (≈10:30),2008\n29.66,Terra (≈10:30),2009\n28.172,Terra (≈10:30),2010\n29.322,Terra (≈10:30),2011\n29.975,Terra (≈10:30),2012\n28.701,Terra (≈10:30),2013\n29.094,Terra (≈10:30),2014\n30.505,Terra (≈10:30),2015\n27.997,Terra (≈10:30),2016\n28.92,Terra (≈10:30),2017\n29.874,Terra (≈10:30),2018\n30.532,Terra (≈10:30),2019\n28.943,Terra (≈10:30),2020\n29.029,Terra (≈10:30),2021\n27.671,Terra (≈10:30),2022\n29.25,Terra (≈10:30),2023\n28.097,Terra (≈10:30),2024\n31.989,Aqua (≈13:30),2003\n31.182,Aqua (≈13:30),2004\n29.842,Aqua (≈13:30),2005\n32.351,Aqua (≈13:30),2006\n31.023,Aqua (≈13:30),2007\n31.836,Aqua (≈13:30),2008\n31.374,Aqua (≈13:30),2009\n29.265,Aqua (≈13:30),2010\n31.253,Aqua (≈13:30),2011\n32.113,Aqua (≈13:30),2012\n30.398,Aqua (≈13:30),2013\n30.676,Aqua (≈13:30),2014\n32.777,Aqua (≈13:30),2015\n29.134,Aqua (≈13:30),2016\n30.531,Aqua (≈13:30),2017\n31.65,Aqua (≈13:30),2018\n32.792,Aqua (≈13:30),2019\n30.272,Aqua (≈13:30),2020\n30.535,Aqua (≈13:30),2021\n29.01,Aqua (≈13:30),2022\n31.692,Aqua (≈13:30),2023\n30.245,Aqua (≈13:30),2024\n\"\"\"\ndf = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(DATA))\n\ndef plot_lst(df):\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7.4, 3.4))\n    for (s, d), c in zip(df.groupby(\"sensor\"), [\"#e67e22\", \"#2a78d6\"]):\n        d = d.sort_values(\"year\")\n        slope, icpt, _, _ = stats.theilslopes(d.lst, d.year)\n        ax.plot(d.year, d.lst, \"o-\", ms=3, color=c,\n                label=f\"{s}: {slope * 10:+.2f} °C per decade\")\n        ax.plot(d.year, icpt + slope * d.year, color=c, lw=1, ls=\"--\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"Dry-season daytime LST, West Java mean (°C)\")\n    ax.set_title(\"T15: two satellites, two trends; the difference is the thesis\",\n                 loc=\"left\", fontsize=10)\n    ax.legend(frameon=False, fontsize=8)\n    return fig\n\nplot_lst(df)\nplt.show()\n"
